<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Bomb costs under Combat Extended, whose bombs are items with their real weight: 227 kg for a Mk. 82, 907 kg for a
    Mk. 84. Stock, they were made from about 33 kg and 70 kg of materials. Without CE the jet loads bombs from steel and
    none of this applies: everything sits inside one guard on something only the Harrier's CE patch sets (the Mk. 82's
    227 kg).

    The case is a bomb case of our own (0.6.0, owner's choice, 7 Nov 2026), one per bomb: the Mk. 82 case and the Mk. 84
    case, each made from steel at the machining table, and at Dead Man's Switch - Expedition's rotary forger when that
    exists. It replaced RimThunder's heavy casting, which doesn't stack: each casting took a whole slot of a VFE Factory
    hopper, so the automated machining bays clogged on them. The cases stack to 4 (agent default), and VFE Factory gives
    the machining bay a bill for each of them by itself, because they are made at the machining table.

    Case weights are the real ones (secondary sources in docs/development/vehicle-patches.md): 140 kg and 478 kg, so 280
    and 956 steel at 0.5 kg a unit. Work 1,000 and 3,000, what the 2 and 6 castings took before. Skill as the bombs that
    use them. No research of their own: the bombs keep theirs. Everything else is AUTHORED.

    Real fill weights are sourced: 87 kg and 429 kg. The Mk. 82 and the incendiary fall short of their weight on purpose
    (owner's choice, 2 Nov 2026): matching it took 174 FSX or 858 prometheum, far too much play time to make, so chemfuel
    carries most of the fill. They share one ratio per kg of real fill: about 0.23 of the scarce ingredient and 3.5
    chemfuel. The EMP, smoke and tox fills have no real equivalent to source.

    The Mk. 84 fills come in canisters of their own (0.20.0, owner's choice, 17 Nov 2026): five incendiary fills, or eight
    smoke fills, EMP coil packs or tox fills, each made in a short bill at the machining table or the ammunition fabricator.
    Before, a Mk. 84 took 14 to 20 hauling trips at once, and Dead Man's Switch's fabricator drops everything it has loaded
    when a haul is interrupted (Fortified's JobDriver_DoAutonomousBill, read 17 Nov 2026), so none was ever finished. Now
    each bill is two or three trips. The materials in all are the same as before; canister counts, masses, bulk, the 500
    work a fill and the fires a store of incendiary or smoke fill makes are AUTHORED.

    MarketValue is removed from the bombs and never set on the cases, so the game works it out from the ingredients, its
    normal rule for made items (StatWorker_MarketValue). Change a number here to rescale a bomb.

    The Mk. 82 case and the Mk. 82's recipe moved to Mods/AircraftMunitions/Patches/Munitions_Shared.xml in 0.37.0, unchanged, so
    they apply with Close Air Support's A-10 alone too, which loads the same Mk. 82; the figures above still describe them.

    The cases were PhobosBombCaseMk82 and PhobosBombCaseMk84 until 0.14.2. An item's defName must not end in a digit (the game
    reads its ID from the digits at the end of name + number), so they were renamed; BombCaseRename.cs carries older saves across.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <!-- The Harrier's own Mk. 82 since 26 Nov 2026 (0.45.1; FWA_Bomb500lb, shared with Close Air Support, before). -->
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="HFW_Bomb500lb"]/statBases[Mass="227"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- The Mk. 84 case. Added as a Def here so it exists only under CE, where the bombs use it. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs</xpath>
          <value>
            <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
              <defName>PhobosBombMk84Case</defName>
              <label>Mk. 84 bomb case</label>
              <description>The empty steel body of a 2,000 lb Mk. 84 bomb: forged and machined, with no filling, fuze or fins yet. Filling and finishing it makes the bomb. Several stack together.</description>
              <graphicData>
                <texPath>Phobos/VehiclePatches/BombCaseMk84</texPath>
                <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
              </graphicData>
              <stackLimit>4</stackLimit>
              <smeltable>true</smeltable>
              <statBases>
                <MaxHitPoints>300</MaxHitPoints>
                <Mass>478</Mass>
                <Bulk>40</Bulk>
                <Flammability>0</Flammability>
                <WorkToMake>3000</WorkToMake>
              </statBases>
              <thingCategories>
                <li>Manufactured</li>
              </thingCategories>
              <costList>
                <Steel>956</Steel>
              </costList>
              <recipeMaker>
                <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
                <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
                <effectWorking>Smith</effectWorking>
                <soundWorking>Recipe_Machining</soundWorking>
                <recipeUsers>
                  <li>TableMachining</li>
                </recipeUsers>
                <skillRequirements>
                  <Crafting>7</Crafting>
                </skillRequirements>
              </recipeMaker>
            </ThingDef>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!--
          The case at the rotary forger too, while Dead Man's Switch - Expedition provides it. The forger runs ordinary
          recipes (Fortified.Building_WorkTableAutonomous, read 3 and 6 Nov 2026), so naming it is all it takes. The
          RecipeDefs are generated after patches, from these recipeUsers. A sequence step that fails ends the sequence,
          hence success Always.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="DMSE_TableLathe"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="PhobosBombMk84Case"]/recipeMaker/recipeUsers</xpath>
            <value>
              <li>DMSE_TableLathe</li>
            </value>
          </match>
        </li>

        <!-- Mk. 84 incendiary, 907 kg: 604 kg of materials, short on purpose (see the header). -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_Incendiary"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
            <operations>
              <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                <xpath>Defs</xpath>
                <value>
                  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
                    <defName>PhobosBombFillIncendiary</defName>
                    <label>incendiary bomb fill</label>
                    <description>A sealed canister of chemfuel thickened with prometheum: a fifth of the fill of a Mk. 84 incendiary bomb. Five of them, a bomb case and the fuzing make the bomb. It burns fiercely, and a store of them can go up in a fire.</description>
                    <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
                    <graphicData>
                      <texPath>Phobos/VehiclePatches/BombFillIncendiary</texPath>
                      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
                    </graphicData>
                    <stackLimit>10</stackLimit>
                    <statBases>
                      <MaxHitPoints>80</MaxHitPoints>
                      <Mass>25</Mass>
                      <Bulk>5</Bulk>
                      <Flammability>2.0</Flammability>
                      <WorkToMake>500</WorkToMake>
                    </statBases>
                    <thingCategories>
                      <li>Manufactured</li>
                    </thingCategories>
                    <costList>
                      <Prometheum>20</Prometheum>
                      <Chemfuel>300</Chemfuel>
                    </costList>
                    <recipeMaker>
                      <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
                      <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
                      <effectWorking>Smith</effectWorking>
                      <soundWorking>Recipe_Machining</soundWorking>
                      <recipeUsers>
                        <li>TableMachining</li>
                      </recipeUsers>
                      <researchPrerequisites>
                        <li>IEDs</li>
                      </researchPrerequisites>
                      <skillRequirements>
                        <Crafting>5</Crafting>
                      </skillRequirements>
                    </recipeMaker>
                    <comps>
                      <li Class="CompProperties_Explosive">
                        <explosiveRadius>1.5</explosiveRadius>
                        <explosiveDamageType>Flame</explosiveDamageType>
                        <explosiveExpandPerStackcount>0.3</explosiveExpandPerStackcount>
                        <startWickOnDamageTaken>
                          <li>Flame</li>
                        </startWickOnDamageTaken>
                        <startWickHitPointsPercent>0.333</startWickHitPointsPercent>
                        <preExplosionSpawnThingDef>Filth_Fuel</preExplosionSpawnThingDef>
                        <preExplosionSpawnChance>1</preExplosionSpawnChance>
                        <wickTicks>70~150</wickTicks>
                      </li>
                    </comps>
                  </ThingDef>
                </value>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
                <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_Incendiary"]/costList</xpath>
                <value>
                  <costList>
                    <PhobosBombMk84Case>1</PhobosBombMk84Case>
                    <PhobosBombFillIncendiary>5</PhobosBombFillIncendiary>
                    <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
                  </costList>
                </value>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
                <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_Incendiary"]/statBases/MarketValue</xpath>
              </li>
            </operations>
          </match>
        </li>

        <!-- Mk. 84 EMP, 907 kg. The steel stands for the coils and ballast of the device. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_EMP"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
            <operations>
              <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                <xpath>Defs</xpath>
                <value>
                  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
                    <defName>PhobosBombCoilEMP</defName>
                    <label>EMP bomb coil pack</label>
                    <description>A wound coil and its ballast for an EMP bomb: an eighth of the device inside a Mk. 84 EMP bomb. Eight of them, a bomb case and the electronics make the bomb.</description>
                    <graphicData>
                      <texPath>Phobos/VehiclePatches/BombCoilEMP</texPath>
                      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
                    </graphicData>
                    <stackLimit>10</stackLimit>
                    <statBases>
                      <MaxHitPoints>80</MaxHitPoints>
                      <Mass>53</Mass>
                      <Bulk>6</Bulk>
                      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
                      <WorkToMake>500</WorkToMake>
                    </statBases>
                    <thingCategories>
                      <li>Manufactured</li>
                    </thingCategories>
                    <costList>
                      <Steel>105</Steel>
                    </costList>
                    <recipeMaker>
                      <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
                      <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
                      <effectWorking>Smith</effectWorking>
                      <soundWorking>Recipe_Machining</soundWorking>
                      <recipeUsers>
                        <li>TableMachining</li>
                      </recipeUsers>
                      <researchPrerequisites>
                        <li>MicroelectronicsBasics</li>
                      </researchPrerequisites>
                      <skillRequirements>
                        <Crafting>5</Crafting>
                      </skillRequirements>
                    </recipeMaker>
                  </ThingDef>
                </value>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
                <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_EMP"]/costList</xpath>
                <value>
                  <costList>
                    <PhobosBombMk84Case>1</PhobosBombMk84Case>
                    <PhobosBombCoilEMP>8</PhobosBombCoilEMP>
                    <ComponentIndustrial>12</ComponentIndustrial>
                  </costList>
                </value>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
                <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_EMP"]/statBases/MarketValue</xpath>
              </li>
            </operations>
          </match>
        </li>

        <!-- Mk. 84 smoke, 907 kg. The steel stands for the smoke canisters inside. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_Smoke"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
            <operations>
              <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                <xpath>Defs</xpath>
                <value>
                  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
                    <defName>PhobosBombFillSmoke</defName>
                    <label>smoke bomb fill</label>
                    <description>A canister of smoke mixture in a steel liner: an eighth of the fill of a Mk. 84 smoke bomb. Eight of them, a bomb case and the fuzing make the bomb. It burns, and a store of them can go up in a fire.</description>
                    <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
                    <graphicData>
                      <texPath>Phobos/VehiclePatches/BombFillSmoke</texPath>
                      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
                    </graphicData>
                    <stackLimit>10</stackLimit>
                    <statBases>
                      <MaxHitPoints>80</MaxHitPoints>
                      <Mass>54</Mass>
                      <Bulk>6</Bulk>
                      <Flammability>1.0</Flammability>
                      <WorkToMake>500</WorkToMake>
                    </statBases>
                    <thingCategories>
                      <li>Manufactured</li>
                    </thingCategories>
                    <costList>
                      <Steel>95</Steel>
                      <Chemfuel>125</Chemfuel>
                    </costList>
                    <recipeMaker>
                      <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
                      <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
                      <effectWorking>Smith</effectWorking>
                      <soundWorking>Recipe_Machining</soundWorking>
                      <recipeUsers>
                        <li>TableMachining</li>
                      </recipeUsers>
                      <researchPrerequisites>
                        <li>SmokepopBelt</li>
                      </researchPrerequisites>
                      <skillRequirements>
                        <Crafting>5</Crafting>
                      </skillRequirements>
                    </recipeMaker>
                    <comps>
                      <li Class="CompProperties_Explosive">
                        <explosiveRadius>1.1</explosiveRadius>
                        <explosiveDamageType>Flame</explosiveDamageType>
                        <explosiveExpandPerStackcount>0.15</explosiveExpandPerStackcount>
                        <startWickOnDamageTaken>
                          <li>Flame</li>
                        </startWickOnDamageTaken>
                        <startWickHitPointsPercent>0.333</startWickHitPointsPercent>
                        <preExplosionSpawnThingDef>Filth_Fuel</preExplosionSpawnThingDef>
                        <preExplosionSpawnChance>1</preExplosionSpawnChance>
                        <wickTicks>70~150</wickTicks>
                      </li>
                    </comps>
                  </ThingDef>
                </value>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
                <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_Smoke"]/costList</xpath>
                <value>
                  <costList>
                    <PhobosBombMk84Case>1</PhobosBombMk84Case>
                    <PhobosBombFillSmoke>8</PhobosBombFillSmoke>
                    <ComponentIndustrial>1</ComponentIndustrial>
                  </costList>
                </value>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
                <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_Smoke"]/statBases/MarketValue</xpath>
              </li>
            </operations>
          </match>
        </li>

        <!-- Mk. 84 poison gas, 907 kg. Exists only with Biotech. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_ToxGas"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
            <operations>
              <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
                <xpath>Defs</xpath>
                <value>
                  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
                    <defName>PhobosBombFillToxGas</defName>
                    <label>tox bomb fill</label>
                    <description>A sealed canister packed with the contents of nine wastepacks: an eighth of the fill of a Mk. 84 tox bomb. Eight of them, a bomb case and the fuzing make the bomb.</description>
                    <graphicData>
                      <texPath>Phobos/VehiclePatches/BombFillToxGas</texPath>
                      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
                    </graphicData>
                    <stackLimit>10</stackLimit>
                    <statBases>
                      <MaxHitPoints>80</MaxHitPoints>
                      <Mass>54</Mass>
                      <Bulk>30</Bulk>
                      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
                      <WorkToMake>500</WorkToMake>
                    </statBases>
                    <thingCategories>
                      <li>Manufactured</li>
                    </thingCategories>
                    <costList>
                      <Wastepack>9</Wastepack>
                    </costList>
                    <recipeMaker>
                      <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
                      <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
                      <effectWorking>Smith</effectWorking>
                      <soundWorking>Recipe_Machining</soundWorking>
                      <recipeUsers>
                        <li>TableMachining</li>
                      </recipeUsers>
                      <researchPrerequisites>
                        <li>ToxGas</li>
                      </researchPrerequisites>
                      <skillRequirements>
                        <Crafting>5</Crafting>
                      </skillRequirements>
                    </recipeMaker>
                  </ThingDef>
                </value>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
                <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_ToxGas"]/costList</xpath>
                <value>
                  <costList>
                    <PhobosBombMk84Case>1</PhobosBombMk84Case>
                    <PhobosBombFillToxGas>8</PhobosBombFillToxGas>
                    <ComponentIndustrial>1</ComponentIndustrial>
                  </costList>
                </value>
              </li>
              <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
                <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Harrier_Mk84Bomb_ToxGas"]/statBases/MarketValue</xpath>
              </li>
            </operations>
          </match>
        </li>

        <!--
          The fills at Dead Man's Switch's ammunition fabricator too, as the bombs are (Fabricator_HarrierVtol.xml). Here rather
          than in that file, so it runs after the fills exist whatever order the files load in. Their bills are two or three
          trips, which the fabricator finishes: it drops everything it has loaded when a haul is interrupted.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <success>Always</success>
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="DMS_TableAmmoPrinter"]</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <success>Always</success>
            <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="PhobosBombFillIncendiary" or defName="PhobosBombCoilEMP" or defName="PhobosBombFillSmoke" or defName="PhobosBombFillToxGas"]/recipeMaker/recipeUsers</xpath>
            <value>
              <li>DMS_TableAmmoPrinter</li>
            </value>
          </match>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
